{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774044590,"nonce":"BB5HXaoKADvnpTIHzJXoaUGM//8=","title":"PTY deprecation plan — SpawnBackend extraction + channel migration","message":"Tracking issue for the long-term PTY deprecation path.\n\n## Current state\nPTY backend handles Claude, Codex, Gemini, and shell sessions. For Claude, SDK is strictly better. PTY's value is: (1) non-Claude agents, (2) terminal visibility via xterm.js.\n\n## Plan\n\n**Phase 1 (now):** Build MCP channel server (73e0adf). PTY unchanged.\n\n**Phase 2 (channels stabilize):** Extract SpawnBackend from PTY:\n- child_process.spawn() instead of node-pty\n- JSON stdout parsing (normalizers already exist)\n- Process lifecycle management (start, stop, restart with backoff)\n- No terminal emulation, no ring buffer, no WebSocket xterm\n- Used for codex, gemini, shell only\n\n**Phase 3 (channels GA):** Deprecate PTY for Claude sessions:\n- SDK: Mandible-owned Claude sessions (full control)\n- Channel-connected: external Claude CLI sessions (structured bidirectional)\n- SpawnBackend: Mandible-managed codex/gemini (process lifecycle, JSON parsing)\n- Unconnected: legacy/ad-hoc (filesystem observation only)\n\n## Blocked by\n- Channels exiting research preview\n- Channel server (73e0adf) proven stable\n- SpawnBackend extraction validated with codex/gemini","files":null}]}